<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n31206" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Nortĭa</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Nurtĭa</span></b> , ae, f., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a goddess of the
				Volsinii</i>, prob. <i>Fortuna</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">quam alii Sortem asserunt, Nemesimque nonnulli,
					Tychenque quam plures, aut Nortiam,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Mart. Cap. 1, § 88</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">in templo Nortiae Etruscae Deae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					7, 3, 7</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">si Nortia Tusco Favisset,</span>”
				i. e. <i>Sejanus</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Juv.
					10, 74</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Tert. Apol. 24</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
